From ebd96582f1e59959ca64f3549f8e1076d5932cba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:15:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Result screen: no rewards on screen until the chest
 opens; badges rise out of its mouth once, never replayed

Funning (Mac, desktop package 09a1b8e): the reward badges already showed above the closed chest.
floating() let any side reward whose state was already 'claimed' (e.g. a replayed level whose region
tool was taken before) hover over a closed chest. Now, with a chest on the page, nothing of the
rewards (badge, icon, count, name) is placed until that chest is open.

The rise from the chest mouth (existing 0.42 s backOut, 0.09 s stagger, gentle bob) plays only on
the panel shown as the chest opens (tap within CHEST_HANDOFF_MS). A later panel of an already-open
chest (restore / re-entry) shows the badges settled at once, and the rise also follows the wall clock,
so coming back from the background mid-rise lands them in place instead of resuming the animation.
resultDiagnostics() reports floatRise.

reward-background-return (on top of ec0de1f): asserts no reward node active/visible before opening
(across 3 hide/show cycles), badges start at the mouth (below, transparent) and settle above the
chest, positions/opacity unchanged across 3 background cycles after opening (only the 3-pt bob),
plus the replayed-level case (closed chest + already-claimed tool shows nothing; an open chest shown
later is settled with no rise) at 390x844 and 320x568. Fails on the old floating() rule.
